      "writtenOn": "2017-07-19T17:27:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a valid scenario, but prefer EC doesn\u0027t handle this.\n\nWhen system is idle, the display goes off and system enters PC10. Since peripherals are not doing anything , the system actually enters S0ix asserting SLP_S0 . The resume is pretty quick as there is no freeze/unfreezing of threads/process involved. This causes an interrupt storm since the system can enter and exit S0ix back to back resulting in SLP_S0 toggling at a higher pace \n\n(Refer:https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/35568877)\n\nThis is different from the echo freeze path where proper freezing of threads/process are invoked.",
      "parentUuid": "467600d5_ce931a0b",
      "revId": "483042d1d3c61f84babb646c9306d6d927469e57",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
